From ef20a0c0e27fc18bd4d07865b06c081c1a2682ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:20:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 50/53] netstack: several network adapters, also ones that
 appear after start

netstack opens every network.* scheme at start and looks again every
2 s, so an adapter that comes up later (Wi-Fi, USB Ethernet plugged in)
gets its own interface: network.wlan* become wlanN, the others ethN,
wired ones first. netcfg lists the interfaces in ifaces/ and tells its
readers when one is added. The address of the default route's interface
is the first source address for smoltcp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
